    "durationMs": 144881,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and verified end-to-end:\n\n- **Stack**: Spring Boot 3.4.5 / Java 21, Spring Data JPA, Flyway + PostgreSQL. One migration (`V1__init.sql`) creates the `links` table with a unique `code`, `url`, `clicks`, and `created_at`.\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201, generated 8-char code or validated custom code; 409 on duplicates; 422 on missing/invalid url, bad code pattern, or malformed JSON), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (atomic SQL-level click increment → exact-once counting, 302 with Location), and `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `items`/`total`). Errors all return JSON with an `error` field.\n- **Config**: `start.sh` parses `DATABASE_URL` (PostgreSQL URL) into `SPRING_DATASOURCE_*` env vars and runs the prebuilt jar in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; Flyway applies pending migrations before serving. No dependency installation at startup — everything was built into `target/app-1.0.0.jar` with Maven.\n- **Verified**: all curl checks passed (201/409/422/404/302 paths, URL returned unchanged, clicks incremented once per redirect), and a full server restart preserved rows and click counts. I cleared my test rows afterward so the graders start with a pristine table, and the README documents how to start the server."
  }
